-- title:
--   Admissible two-sided learning reward process and the expected SC-PC mismatch
-- statement:
--   On a probability space $(\Omega,\mathbb P)$ let $X_t(i,k)$ be player $i$'s observed utility and $Y_t(k,i)$ arm $k$'s observed utility if $i$ and $k$ are matched in round $t$. Let $\mathcal H_t$ be the $\sigma$-algebra generated by all actions and observations through round $t-1$ together with the round-$t$ proposals and acceptance decisions (since SC-PC is deterministic, it is generated by the record of matched pairs and observed utilities through round $t-1$). The process is **admissible** if
--
--   1. all values lie in $[0,1]$ and are measurable;
--   2. for every round $t$, pair $(i,k)$ and $A\in\mathcal H_t$, with $E=\{i,k\text{ matched in round }t\}$,
--   $$
--   \mathbb E[X_t(i,k)\,\mathbf 1_{A\cap E}]=\mu_{i,k}\,\mathbb P(A\cap E),\qquad \mathbb E[Y_t(k,i)\,\mathbf 1_{A\cap E}]=\pi_{k,i}\,\mathbb P(A\cap E).
--   $$
--
--   No independence or distributional assumption is made. The expected cumulative mismatch of SC-PC is
--   $$
--   \mathbb E[D(T;I)]=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb P\bigl(M_t\ne m^*_t\bigr),
--   $$
--   with $m^*_t$ the POSM of the true mean utilities.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Values off the matched event are never observed, so requiring them in $[0,1]$ and measurable loses no process. Conditioning is on $\mathcal H_t$, not on other owners' current observations. $\mathbb P$ of a set is its outer measure, so `expDpc` cannot collapse to $0$ for lack of measurability.
-- source:
--   J. Chen, M. Gao, Z. Zhang, Decentralized Dynamic Stable Matching, arXiv:2610.41912 (held version, sha256 6a27277e…), §2.2, p.4; §5.1, p.12; App. C.5.1, p.47; eq. (1), p.5

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_DecDynMatch_IsPOSM
import Definitions.Def_DecDynMatch_Supplement_scpcExec

namespace DecDynMatch.Supplement

open DecDynMatch MeasureTheory

variable {K : ℕ} {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω]

/-- The realized matching of SC-PC at sample point `ω`, for player-side rewards
`X t i k : Ω → ℝ` and arm-side rewards `Y t k i : Ω → ℝ`. -/
noncomputable def Momega (I : Instance K ι) (ord : Fin K → ι → ℕ)
    (X : ℕ → ι → Fin K → Ω → ℝ) (Y : ℕ → Fin K → ι → Ω → ℝ) (t : ℕ) (ω : Ω) :
    ι → Option (Fin K) :=
  Mpc I ord (fun s i k => X s i k ω) (fun s k i => Y s k i ω) t

open Classical in
/-- The record of all observations through round `t − 1`: for every round `s < t` and pair
`(i, k)`, whether `i` and `k` were matched and, if so, the two observed utilities
(`(false, 0, 0)` otherwise). -/
noncomputable def obsRecord (I : Instance K ι) (ord : Fin K → ι → ℕ)
    (X : ℕ → ι → Fin K → Ω → ℝ) (Y : ℕ → Fin K → ι → Ω → ℝ) (t : ℕ) (ω : Ω) :
    ℕ → ι → Fin K → Bool × ℝ × ℝ :=
  fun s i k => if s < t ∧ Momega I ord X Y s ω i = some k then (true, X s i k ω, Y s k i ω)
    else (false, 0, 0)

/-- The σ-algebra `H_t` (p.47): generated by all actions and observations through round `t − 1`
together with the round-`t` proposals and acceptance decisions. SC-PC is deterministic given the
observations, so the observation record through round `t − 1` generates it. -/
noncomputable abbrev histSigma (I : Instance K ι) (ord : Fin K → ι → ℕ)
    (X : ℕ → ι → Fin K → Ω → ℝ) (Y : ℕ → Fin K → ι → Ω → ℝ) (t : ℕ) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  MeasurableSpace.comap (obsRecord I ord X Y t) inferInstance

/-- The event that player `i` and arm `k` are matched in round `t`. -/
def matchedEv (I : Instance K ι) (ord : Fin K → ι → ℕ)
    (X : ℕ → ι → Fin K → Ω → ℝ) (Y : ℕ → Fin K → ι → Ω → ℝ) (t : ℕ) (i : ι) (k : Fin K) :
    Set Ω :=
  {ω | Momega I ord X Y t ω i = some k}

/-- **Admissible reward process (two-sided learning).** J. Chen, M. Gao, Z. Zhang, *Decentralized Dynamic Stable Matching*, arXiv:2610.41912
(held version, sha256 6a27277e…), §2.2, p.4: "When player i is matched
with arm k, both sides observe their respective stochastic utilities in [0, 1], with expectations
μ_{i,k} and π_{k,i}, respectively. Rejected proposals yield no utility observations"; §5.1, p.12:
"conditional on all past actions and observations and on the current proposals and acceptance
decisions, the utilities observed by a matched player i and the corresponding arm k, have means
μ_{i,k} and π_{k,i}, respectively"; App. C.5.1, p.47: "an accepted observation from stream x lies in
[0, 1] and has mean θₓ conditional on H_t."

On a probability space `(Ω, P)`, `X t i k ω` is player `i`'s observed utility if it is matched with
arm `k` in round `t`, and `Y t k i ω` is arm `k`'s. `RewardOK I ord P X Y` says: all values lie in
`[0, 1]`; each is measurable; and for every round `t`, pair `(i, k)` and every `A ∈ H_t`,
`E[X t i k; A ∩ {i, k matched in t}] = μ_{i,k} · P(A ∩ {i, k matched in t})`, and likewise
`E[Y t k i; A ∩ {…}] = π_{k,i} · P(A ∩ {…})`.

**Formalization Note.**
* No independence and no distributional assumption is made beyond range and conditional mean.
* Values off the matched event are never observed; requiring them in `[0, 1]` and measurable loses
  no reward process (replace them by `0`).
* The conditioning is on `H_t` only, not on other owners' current observations (p.47). -/
def RewardOK (I : Instance K ι) (ord : Fin K → ι → ℕ) (P : Measure Ω)
    (X : ℕ → ι → Fin K → Ω → ℝ) (Y : ℕ → Fin K → ι → Ω → ℝ) : Prop :=
  (∀ t i k ω, X t i k ω ∈ Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1) ∧ (∀ t k i ω, Y t k i ω ∈ Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1) ∧
  (∀ t i k, Measurable (X t i k)) ∧ (∀ t k i, Measurable (Y t k i)) ∧
  (∀ t i k (A : Set Ω), MeasurableSet[histSigma I ord X Y t] A →
    ∫ ω in A ∩ matchedEv I ord X Y t i k, X t i k ω ∂P =
      I.μ i k * (P (A ∩ matchedEv I ord X Y t i k)).toReal) ∧
  (∀ t i k (A : Set Ω), MeasurableSet[histSigma I ord X Y t] A →
    ∫ ω in A ∩ matchedEv I ord X Y t i k, Y t k i ω ∂P =
      I.π k i * (P (A ∩ matchedEv I ord X Y t i k)).toReal)

/-- **Expected cumulative POSM mismatch of SC-PC.** J. Chen, M. Gao, Z. Zhang, *Decentralized Dynamic Stable Matching*, arXiv:2610.41912
(held version, sha256 6a27277e…), eq. (1), p.5, and p.5: "When protocol
decisions or utility observations are randomized, we consider the expected mismatch cost
E[D_Π(T; I)]."

`expDpc I ord P X Y T = Σ_{t=1}^{T} P(Mₜ is not the POSM of round t)`, the POSM taken with respect to
the true (mean) utilities `I.μ, I.π`.

**Formalization Note.** By linearity `E[D] = Σₜ P(Mₜ ≠ m*ₜ)`. `P` of a set is its outer measure, so
the definition never collapses to `0` for lack of measurability; on measurable events (the case for
every admissible reward process) it is the probability. -/
noncomputable def expDpc (I : Instance K ι) (ord : Fin K → ι → ℕ) (P : Measure Ω)
    (X : ℕ → ι → Fin K → Ω → ℝ) (Y : ℕ → Fin K → ι → Ω → ℝ) (T : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  ∑ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 T, (P {ω | ¬ IsPOSM I t (Momega I ord X Y t ω)}).toReal

end DecDynMatch.Supplement


